jobs.description:
We’re looking for a seasoned and detail-obsessed Full Stack Developer to join the team of one of our clients. In this role, you’ll own features end to end: from translating a Figma design into pixel-perfect UI, to building the secure back-end logic behind it, to shipping it cleanly with your team. The ideal candidate is equally strong in Frontend and Backend, moves fast without cutting corners, and uses AI engineering tools to deliver more, sooner.
Ready to build something great? Let’s see what it takes 💛
What you will do

- Build, refine, and maintain core features across the full stack, ensuring a polished, high-performance user experience;

- Develop and optimize both the company’s main application and its internal Admin Interfaces, including user management and billing systems;

- Implement high-fidelity UI/UX with pixel-perfect execution of product designs, down to the smallest detail;

- Work closely with Product Managers and Designers, turning Figma designs into seamless production code;

- Design and maintain significant, sensitive, and secure back-end logic and infrastructure;

- Collaborate with another developer and the QA team to ensure smooth integration, high code quality, and flawless deployments;

- Maintain and update the company’s marketing website, built on WordPress;

- Leverage AI tools to accelerate the development lifecycle and speed up delivery without compromising quality.

What you need to succeed in this role

- 8+ years of proven experience as a Full Stack Developer, with a strong and balanced track record in both Frontend and Backend;

- Deep, significant experience with React;

- Significant, hands-on experience with Python and Java, and the ability to handle complex and sensitive architecture;

- Proven ability to deliver pixel-perfect UI with a sharp eye for detail, and extensive experience working with Figma;

- Practical experience with WordPress maintenance and customization;

- Excellent teamwork: a track record of working effectively with other developers, QA engineers, and product stakeholders;

- A fast-delivery, highly adaptable mindset, with strong proficiency in AI engineering tools to boost productivity.

Will be a plus

- Experience with Next.js.

Benefits

- Fixed schedule: Sunday–Thursday, 09:00–18:00 (UTC +2) ;

- Fully remote cooperation;

- Cooperation on a fast-growing B2B SaaS product;

- Inclusive and international environment;

- Compensation in USD;

- Trust-based management with no micromanagement, focused on your growth and long-term collaboration.

*The items listed in this section may vary depending on the terms of your engagement. Certain benefits and conditions typically apply to employees; independent contractors may not be eligible for all of these. The specific terms, including compensation, benefits, and work conditions, will be clearly defined in your agreement if selected.
You can learn more about the company and its culture by visiting our official website and social pages on Facebook, Instagram, and LinkedIn.
So if you're a proactive Full Stack Developer who thrives on solving problems, ensuring customer satisfaction, and delivering outstanding service, don't miss this opportunity and send us your CV in English to collaborate with us!
Know someone perfect for the role? Refer them and get rewarded!
We adhere to the principles of equal treatment of candidates and prohibit discrimination on any grounds protected by law.
Your personal data will be processed as described in the SupportYourApp Candidate Privacy Notice .
